Software rendering when asked for

niri rejects a software EGL renderer (llvmpipe), for the problems such a
renderer has beside a GPU's.  A virtual machine on a Mac has no GPU that
draws, and bunix tests its desktop in one (tools/desktop-test.sh): there
niri is started with BUNIX_NIRI_SOFTWARE_RENDERING=1, and draws with
llvmpipe.  Without the variable, niri is as upstream has it.

A software renderer names no render node, and niri then took the
device's primary node for it.  On a GPU that has a render node (virtio's
on the arm64 test machine) the primary GPU was chosen by that one, and
the two did not match: niri ran with no renderer.  The device's own
render node is taken first.  A GPU's EGL device always names its render
node, so this changes nothing for one.

--- a/src/backend/tty.rs
+++ b/src/backend/tty.rs
@@ -784,15 +784,24 @@
             // Software EGL devices (e.g., llvmpipe/softpipe) are rejected for now. They have some
             // problems (segfault on importing dmabufs from other renderers) and need to be
             // excluded from some places like DRM leasing.
+            //
+            // bunix: allowed where BUNIX_NIRI_SOFTWARE_RENDERING=1 says so, which only its
+            // tests of the desktop in a virtual machine do; a machine with no GPU but the
+            // processor has nothing else to draw with.
+            let software_allowed =
+                std::env::var_os("BUNIX_NIRI_SOFTWARE_RENDERING").is_some_and(|value| value == "1");
             ensure!(
-                !egl_device.is_software(),
+                software_allowed || !egl_device.is_software(),
                 "software EGL renderers are skipped"
             );
 
+            // bunix: a software renderer names no render node.  The device's own, where it has
+            // one, is the node the primary GPU was chosen by; only then does it match.
             let render_node = egl_device
                 .try_get_render_node()
                 .ok()
                 .flatten()
+                .or_else(|| node.node_with_type(NodeType::Render).and_then(Result::ok))
                 .unwrap_or(node);
             self.gpu_manager
                 .as_mut()
